  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068112/assets/cb5c201068966a7d25ff3640d478e03a78bc075900181bdee93d5612b0217609.png)\n\nConsider the vector $v$ shown above. Find the vector $Av$ given that \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that $A$ is a rotation-scaling matrix. So, we need to find its scale factor and the angle of rotation.\n\nWe can find the scale factor using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{det(A)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(0)}^{2}+{(3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent $A$ as a product of a rotation and a scaling matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =3[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\\,\u27f9\\,\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ counterclockwise by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$  and scale the result by a scale factor of $3,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068112/assets/7165c52d2280e4a53dc640acdca7671dcb897921028e675a583c46e6ccd40e33.png)",
